  <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
  <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>
```

3. This code creates a container div with an ID of `img-container`, which will hold both the image and its caption. The image is wrapped in an anchor tag (`a`) to make it clickable. Make sure to replace `image.jpg` with the path to your own image, and `http://www.example.com` with the URL you want to link to.

4. Now let's add some styling to our page using CSS. In the head section, add the following style rules:

```css
#img-container {
  text-align: center;
}

#img-container img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

#img-container p {
  margin: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}
```

These styles will:

- Center-align the contents of the `img-container` div
- Set the width of the image to 100% and maintain its aspect ratio by setting its height to `auto`
- Remove the bottom margin from the caption paragraph (`p`)
- Italicize the caption text

5. Save the file and open it in a web browser to see the result. You should now see your image with its caption displayed below it. Click on the image to go to the specified URL.

